<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">José Batlle y Ordóñez</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">1856–1929</span></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">José Batlle y Ordóñez was a Uruguayan journalist and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/colorado">Colorado</a> Party politician, president in 1903–1907 and 1911–1915. He ended the last Blanco revolt in 1904 and built an early welfare state, introducing the eight-hour working day, secular education, divorce reform and state-owned enterprises. He also championed a collegiate executive, adopted in modified form in 1918.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/jose-batlle-y-ordonez.jpg" alt="José Batlle y Ordóñez" width="254" height="359" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:JoseBatlle1900.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
